---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import '../../styles/pages.css';
---

<Site title="Quell Privacy Policy" description="Privacy policy for Quell, the browser extension by Purple Directive.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
    <div class="legal-page">
    <h1>Quell Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Version 2.0.0 · Effective September 26, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Quell is a browser extension by Purple Directive that hides content you did not ask for,
      such as AI answers on search engines, cookie banners and pop-ups. It works inside your
      browser. This policy covers Quell on every browser it is available for. Our website, purpledirective.com, has its own
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      Quell has no analytics, no tracking and no accounts. The only information it sends us is
      a report you choose to send when a site looks broken. The report contains the site's
      domain (for example, shop.example.com) and your Quell version, and Quell shows you both
      before you send it. Because a reported domain comes from your browsing, Quell's store
      listings declare the report as browsing data.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Use It</h2>
    <p>
      We use reports only to find and fix sites Quell breaks. We never use them for anything
      unrelated to Quell.
    </p>

    <h2>Who We Share It With</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell reports or share them with anyone, other than the hosting provider that
      runs our report server.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Settings</h2>
    <p>
      Your choices are saved in your browser's extension storage. Some browsers can sync
      extension settings across your devices when you are signed in; if yours does, that
      syncing is handled by your browser under its own privacy terms, and we never receive it.
      A few settings and a count of hidden items always stay on the device. Uninstalling Quell
      removes its settings from your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Site Access</h2>
    <p>
      Quell works on two major search engines' result pages from the start. It asks for access to other
      sites only when you turn on a feature that needs it, such as other search engines,
      cookie banners or pop-ups, and it gives broad site access back when you turn those
      features off. It looks at pages only to decide what to hide, does that on your device,
      and sends nothing from them. If you turn on "Say reject all for me", Quell presses the
      reject button on consent banners it recognizes and lets those consent tools load so they
      can record your choice.
    </p>
    <p>
      Apart from a report you choose to send, Quell makes no network requests of its own. Its
      block lists ship inside the extension and update with it. Versions before 0.6.0 send
      nothing at all.
    </p>

    <h2>How Long We Keep It</h2>
    <p>
      Reports are stored as counts per site, per version, per day, and are deleted after 180
      days. Our report server does not keep IP addresses.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>Reports are sent over an encrypted connection and hold nothing that identifies you.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Quell is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their information.</p>

    <h2>Your Choices</h2>
    <p>
      Sending a report is always optional, and you can use every feature without ever sending
      one. Because reports carry no identifier, we cannot link a report to you, but you can
      ask us any question about your data at the address below.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and Contact</h2>
    <p>
      When this policy changes, we will post the new version here with a new version number
      and effective date, and note material changes in the extension's changelog. Questions:
      <Fragment set:html={'<!--email_off--><a href="mailto:support@purpledirective.com">support@purpledirective.com</a><!--/email_off-->'} />.
    </p>
    </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 680px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) 0;
  }

  .legal-page h1 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .legal-page h2 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .legal-page h2:first-of-type {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .legal-page p,
  .legal-page li {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-page ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin: var(--spacing-sm) 0;
  }

  .legal-page li {
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .legal-page a {
    color: var(--purple-primary);
  }

  .legal-page code {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    background: var(--bg-tinted);
    padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
</style>
